# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Engine outputs (docs/output-contract.md). Ignored by DEFAULT (regenerated each
# run off the shared cache) EXCEPT the three real groups below — GitHub Pages
# serves from docs/ on main, so their standings/projection/timeline JSON MUST be
# committed or the live site is empty. Any other/experimental group's output
# stays ignored until it is explicitly un-ignored here.
docs/data/*/standings.json
docs/data/*/projection.json
docs/data/*/timeline.json
!docs/data/panel/standings.json
!docs/data/panel/projection.json
!docs/data/panel/timeline.json
!docs/data/family/standings.json
!docs/data/family/projection.json
!docs/data/family/timeline.json
!docs/data/church/standings.json
!docs/data/church/projection.json
!docs/data/church/timeline.json
!docs/data/browns/standings.json
!docs/data/browns/projection.json
!docs/data/browns/timeline.json
# Test fixture output — a synthetic replay group, never committed to history.
docs/data/test/

# Commentary intermediates (groups/<group>/output/). Split by overwrite-vs-
# accumulate (playbook rule 5): week_packet.json and the dry-run prompt preview
# are REGENERATED from committed engine output every run, so they are ignored —
# committing them would just be a second copy of docs/data/<group>/ that can
# drift. The filed columns and column_memory.json ACCUMULATE (season-long
# continuity the pundit reads back), so they stay tracked.
groups/*/output/week_packet.json
groups/*/output/commentary_prompt_preview.txt
# Drafts the factual guard refused (scripts/column_guard.py). They are kept on
# disk deliberately -- a rejected draft is the evidence for whatever prompt or
# scan change comes next, and reading it is the only way to tell a real
# fabrication from a rule that needs loosening. But they are NOT columns: they
# were never filed, never indexed and never appended to column_memory.json, and
# committing one would put prose in the tree that the site does not serve and
# next week's prompt must never read back as an exemplar.
groups/*/output/column_week_*.rejected.md

# Multi-year backtest cache for calibrate_spread.py. Fetched from CFBD on demand
# (data/backtest_cache/{lines,sp,games}.json), regenerable with --refresh. Kept
# OUT of the repo and OUT of the season-guarded production cache (data/cfbd_cache.json).
data/backtest_cache/

# Owner-portrait generator (scripts/generate_owner_images.py) — privacy:
# real photos of friends and un-approved generated art never get committed.
# A chosen winner is manually copied into docs/assets/portraits/.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. A bare `output/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed groups/<group>/output/ — so
# the filed columns and column_memory.json the block above declares "stay
# tracked" were in fact unstageable, and every generated column would have died
# with the CI runner. generate_owner_images.py writes to ROOT/output/personas
# (its --out default) and repo-root output/ is the only such directory, so the
# leading slash costs nothing and restores the intended scope.
assets/source_photos/
/output/*
# ...except the framing sidecars, which are not art and carry no photo. Both
# are hand-authored maps of percentages -- focal.json is filename ->
# object-position, faces.json is filename -> [top%, bottom%] of the face band
# -- read at publish time and copied into docs/data/<group>/banners.json. The
# manifest REGENERATES in full on every build (playbook rule 5), so a sidecar
# that only ever lived on one laptop means the next person to re-run
# build_banners.py silently republishes every banner on the default crop and
# puts the faces back under the fold, and drops the measurement the cap floor
# is checked against. The privacy reason this whole block exists -- real
# photos, un-approved art -- does not reach a file of percentages.
#
# alt.json is deliberately NOT here. It has the same exposure and arguably
# belongs, but it predates this exception and changing its status is a call
# for whoever owns the alt-text pass, not a side effect of a framing branch.
!/output/banners/
/output/banners/*
!/output/banners/*/
/output/banners/*/*
!/output/banners/*/focal.json
!/output/banners/*/faces.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output (screenshots, console logs, a11y snapshots)
# written into the repo root during browser verification runs. Throwaway.
.playwright-mcp/

# Screenshot-gate captures. The visual verification pass every front-end thread
# runs shoots each page at a desktop and a mobile width via Playwright MCP's
# browser_take_screenshot, and a call that passes an explicit `filename` writes
# it to the CWD -- which is the repo root, NOT .playwright-mcp/ above. That is
# where an-panel-1440.png, index-390.png and managers-1440.png keep coming
# from. They are regenerable by re-running the gate, are an input to nothing,
# and sit right where a careless `git add .` will take them.
#
# SERVE THE SITE FOR THAT PASS WITH `python scripts/shotserve.py`, never with
# a bare `python -m http.server` on a fixed port. A leftover server on a shared
# port once served a whole pass from a pre-branch checkout and every one of
# the resulting captures was of the wrong tree; shotserve takes a free port
# and proves what it serves matches disk before handing back a URL. Its
# docstring has the incident in full, and scripts/test_server_ownership.py
# plus the PreToolUse hook keep it from being worked around.
#
# Two shapes, because the gate produces two:
#   <page>-<width>.<ext>   the convention the gate uses when it names a file;
#                          3+ digits, so a WxH suffix (390x844) matches too and
#                          an ordinary name like logo-v2.png does not.
#   page-<timestamp>.<ext> the tool's OWN default, used by any call that passes
#                          no filename at all.
#
# ANCHORED for the reason spelled out at the /output/ block above: unanchored,
# these would match at any depth and could swallow a real asset that happens to
# carry a width suffix -- docs/assets/ is full of generated art and nothing
# stops a future one being named that way. The repo root is the only scratch
# level here; every directory below it holds files somebody meant to keep. If a
# genuine root-level image ever needs committing, `git add -f` is the escape
# hatch and is the right amount of friction.
/*-[0-9][0-9][0-9]*.png
/*-[0-9][0-9][0-9]*.jpg
/*-[0-9][0-9][0-9]*.jpeg
/*-[0-9][0-9][0-9]*.webp
/page-*.png
/page-*.jpg
/page-*.jpeg
/page-*.webp

# Figma export of the site design — a large binary design INPUT, not source.
# Kept local; the built site it informed lives in docs/.
assets/Figma site code/

# Per-run API request tally (CLAUDE.md rule 6): cumulative daily count that
# resets on the UTC date rollover. Runtime state, rewritten by every
# generation run — it persists on disk, which is all the budget guard needs.
data/gemini_budget.json
